// OSL port: src/liboslexec/opnoise.cpp
//
// The extern "C" noise entry points the generated shader code calls (cellnoise, hashnoise, noise, snoise, simplexnoise, usimplexnoise, nullnoise, unullnoise
// and the periodic, generic and gabor forms), plus the NoiseParams setters and the osl_hash_* functions. The math is in oslnoise.cs, gabornoise.cs and
// simplexnoise.cs. This file is generated by a script from the NOISE_IMPL / NOISE_IMPL_DERIV / PNOISE_IMPL / ... macro tables of opnoise.cpp.
//
// Not ported: osl_count_noise (needs the ShadingContext). The sg argument of the generic entry points is only used by the C++ to report an unknown noise
// name through the error handler; here that is reported to unknown_noise_type_hook (a null hook means the result is left untouched, as in the C++).

